---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Caring for Aging Parents"
  description="Plain-language privacy policy: no cookies or tracking by default on our website, and secure payment and file delivery handled by Gumroad."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Privacy Policy", href: "/privacy/" }]}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="prose-measure space-y-8">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-teal">
        Privacy policy (in plain language)
      </h1>

      <p class="text-ink">
        We built <strong>{siteConfig.name}</strong> for families who value calm, straightforward tools and personal privacy. Here is exactly how this website works and how your information is handled.
      </p>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          1. No cookies and no tracking by default on this website
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          When you browse the pages on <strong>{siteConfig.url}</strong>, we do not set tracking cookies, we do not run advertising popups, and analytics scripts are turned off by default. You can read our guides and browse our printable sheets without being tracked across the internet.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          This website is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any website host, Cloudflare handles ordinary technical information, such as your IP address and browser type, to deliver pages and keep them secure. We do not use that information to identify you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          2. We never ask for sensitive personal details
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          There are no user accounts, login passwords, or intake forms on this website. We will never ask you for passwords, bank account numbers, government ID numbers, or health details.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          3. How Gumroad handles payments and PDF delivery
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          When you click a button to download our free sample or buy a printable PDF pack, you leave this website and complete your order on <strong>Gumroad</strong>, our digital checkout provider.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-ink">
          <li>
            Gumroad processes your payment securely and sends an email with the download link for your PDF files.
          </li>
          <li>
            We never see or store your full credit card number.
          </li>
          <li>
            Gumroad has its own privacy policy, which you can read at <a href="https://gumroad.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">gumroad.com/privacy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            Gumroad shares your email address and the name of the product you ordered with us on our seller receipt record so we can help you if you ever lose your download link.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          4. Emails from us
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          If you download the free sample or buy a printable, Gumroad holds your email address. We may send you occasional emails through Gumroad about new printables. Every one of those emails has an unsubscribe link, and you can also ask us at the address below to remove you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-teal">
          5. If you write to us
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-ink">
          The form on our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> does not send or store your message. It only prepares an email in your own email app or webmail, and nothing reaches us until you press Send there. If you write to us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>, we use your email address only to reply to you. We never sell, rent, or trade your email address with anyone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-muted">
        Last updated: 11 November 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
